# Seller Support Triage Console — what is NOT committed
#
# Policy: code only, for now. All prose, data artefacts and the archived corpus
# stay local. README.md gets written and committed when the project is
# finalised — until then this repo is source, not documentation.
#
# TWO THINGS TO KNOW BEFORE EDITING THIS FILE:
#
# 1. Git does NOT support trailing comments. `foo.json  # why` is read as a
#    literal pattern including the spaces and the hash, and silently matches
#    nothing. Comments go on their own line. (This bit us once already.)
#
# 2. Data files are excluded BY NAME, not by extension glob. A blanket
#    `*.json` / `*.txt` would silently swallow package.json, tsconfig.json and
#    requirements.txt the moment the console UI lands. Add new artefacts by name.

# ── Prose ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every .md: the handoff, the knowledge base writeup, the planning notes and
# the per-module READMEs. README.md is deliberately included in this —
# un-ignore it with `!README.md` when the finalised one is ready to commit.
*.md

# ── Generated documents and diagrams ─────────────────────────────────────
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# ── The archived corpus ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 594 scraped first-party Amazon documents, their PDFs and the embedding
# caches, ~5.8 MB. Two reasons beyond size: it is Amazon's content, not ours
# to republish, and build_corpus.py regenerates it.
SellerSupport_Docs/

# ── Data artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# COMMITTED DELIBERATELY, despite being data: chunks.jsonl (3.8 MB) and
# opensearch/synonyms.txt. local_search.py reads both directly, so without
# them a clone is 26 scripts that cannot run. They are the difference between
# a repo someone can read and a system someone can start.
#
# Everything below is regenerable by the script named above it.
# reembed_bedrock.py — the local-embedding fallback copy
chunks.local-bge.jsonl
# semantic_filter.py — the frozen 45-document knowledge base
knowledge_base.json
# the 67 plain-language tickets that selected the corpus
filter_queries.tsv
# embedding caches, keyed to a corpus fingerprint
*.npz

# ── Retrieval baselines ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
opensearch/evaluate_baseline.json

# ── The corpus audit trail ───────────────────────────────────────────────
claude_reference_CSA/

# ── Runtime output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pipeline/decision_trail.jsonl
pipeline/precedents.jsonl
opensearch/evaluate_results.json
opensearch/index_mapping.json
opensearch/search_pipeline.json

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# ── Local and sensitive ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
.aws/
*.pem
*.key
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude desktop app launch config, local tooling only
.claude/
